USC: integer MOVCBIT/ATOM_CMPXCHG on cores with the vector instruction set

The integer converter hands MOVCBIT and ATOM_CMPXCHG to
ConvertComparisonInstructionF32, which used the scalar F32 register
accessors.  On SGX543/544 integer registers live in vector registers, so a
select whose operand came from a plain copy read the wrong register and the
result was taken from a stale scratch register: e.g. "c ? a : b" became
"b" with no diagnostic.  Use the typeless (unpack/pack) accessors for these
opcodes, as the rest of the integer converter does, and do the same for the
duplicate-channel moves in ConvertBitwiseInstructionF32.

ATOM_CMPXCHG also tested (old ^ compare) with the float MOVC, which treats
-0 and denormal bit patterns as zero, so the exchange could happen when the
values differ.  Use the 32-bit integer MOVC.

